### (3/3) Pass only the remaining budget

**Severity:** `medium`

The existing `SendMessageTimeoutW` call receives the full timeout on every ancestor, so several slow-but-responsive windows can keep the low-level mouse hook waiting for multiple timeout periods. Compute the remaining time from the shared deadline before each send and stop once it expires; this must be applied with the deadline setup in (1/3) and (2/3).

```suggestion
        const ULONGLONG now = GetTickCount64();
        if (now >= deadline)
        {
            return nullptr;
        }

        const UINT remainingTimeoutMs = static_cast<UINT>(deadline - now);
        if (!SendMessageTimeoutW(
                hwnd,
                WM_NCHITTEST,
                0,
                MAKELPARAM(local.x, local.y),
                SMTO_ABORTIFHUNG,
                remainingTimeoutMs,
                &hit))
```

### Check the root hit-test after a child returns `HTCLIENT`

**Severity:** `medium`

When `WindowFromPoint` returns a child control, this loop stops on `HTCLIENT` without asking the root window for its non-client hit-test. A custom title bar can report `HTCAPTION` for its drag region only from the root, so right-dragging over an `HTCLIENT` child in that region is missed even though the top-level window identifies it as draggable. Query the root once for this child result before returning `nullptr`.

```suggestion
        if (hitTest == HTCLIENT && hwnd != root)
        {
            // A custom title bar may define its drag region only in the root window.
            hwnd = root;
            continue;
        }
        if (hitTest != HTTRANSPARENT || hwnd == root)
```
